From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Tetar <gabriel@intercreate.io>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 01:06:14 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] usb: usb_c: tc: accept -ENOTSUP when disabling VCONN

A TCPC without a VCONN supply reports tcpc_set_vconn() as -ENOTSUP:
the STM32 UCPD driver does so when no VCONN control callback is
registered. tc_init() already accepts it, but the CC-open entry and the
Attached.SRC exit accept only -ENOSYS. In a source-capable build on
such a TCPC every ErrorRecovery entry therefore logged an error,
requested ErrorRecovery again and returned before opening the CC lines,
so the port kept presenting Rp through tErrorRecovery, and every source
detach logged "Couldn't disable VCONN source".

Accept -ENOTSUP in both places, as tc_init() does.

Signed-off-by: Gabriel Tetar <gabriel@intercreate.io>
---
 subsys/usb/usb_c/usbc_tc_common.c     | 2 +-
 subsys/usb/usb_c/usbc_tc_src_states.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/subsys/usb/usb_c/usbc_tc_common.c b/subsys/usb/usb_c/usbc_tc_common.c
index 6a41686c9d9..84c0aecda39 100644
--- a/subsys/usb/usb_c/usbc_tc_common.c
+++ b/subsys/usb/usb_c/usbc_tc_common.c
@@ -288,7 +288,7 @@ static void tc_cc_open_entry(void *obj)
 	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_USBC_CSM_SUPPORTS_SOURCE)) {
 		/* Disable VCONN */
 		ret = tcpc_set_vconn(tcpc, false);
-		if (ret != 0 && ret != -ENOSYS) {
+		if (ret != 0 && ret != -ENOSYS && ret != -ENOTSUP) {
 			LOG_ERR("Couldn't disable vconn: %d", ret);
 			tc_set_state(dev, TC_ERROR_RECOVERY_STATE);
 			return;
diff --git a/subsys/usb/usb_c/usbc_tc_src_states.c b/subsys/usb/usb_c/usbc_tc_src_states.c
index cacb32d162b..b35e6f8c5b9 100644
--- a/subsys/usb/usb_c/usbc_tc_src_states.c
+++ b/subsys/usb/usb_c/usbc_tc_src_states.c
@@ -355,7 +355,7 @@ void tc_attached_src_exit(void *obj)
 
 	/* Stop sourcing VCONN */
 	ret = tcpc_set_vconn(tcpc, false);
-	if (ret != 0 && ret != -ENOSYS) {
+	if (ret != 0 && ret != -ENOSYS && ret != -ENOTSUP) {
 		LOG_ERR("Couldn't disable VCONN source");
 	}
 }
